# Build output, dependencies, lock files.
node_modules/
dist/
target/
pnpm-lock.yaml
Cargo.lock

# Generated from the .ai/ modules by `cargo xtask sync-agents`. Formatting it here would
# make it differ from what the generator produces, and `sync-agents --check` is part of
# the gate — so Prettier and the gate would fight each other on every commit.
AGENTS.md

# Golden parity data. `tests/golden/reference/` holds the archived legacy
# implementation's real output, compared byte for byte by
# `crates/codepack-engine/tests/golden.rs`; `tests/golden/fixtures/` holds the inputs that
# produced it. Reformatting either would rewrite the thing under test — the exact bytes
# are the assertion.
tests/golden/

# Per-crate test fixtures, for the same reason: file contents feed byte counts, token
# estimates, and scanner findings that tests assert on exactly.
crates/*/tests/fixtures/

# Markdown stays hand-written. The documents in `.ai/`, `docs/`, `BLUEPRINT.md`, and
# `ROADMAP.md` are hand-wrapped prose with wide reference tables; Prettier would rewrite
# the table alignment and fight the wrap style the project's own rules describe. Prose is
# reviewed by humans, and a formatter adds nothing there.
*.md
